<h1>Define Sphere</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<table class="NormalTable" style="border-spacing:0px;" cellspacing="0">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs4">
<td valign="top" class="whs5">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../Images/image025.gif" width="203px" height="198px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs7">
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Capture</b></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US">– for delayed definition of a datum sphere by probe capture.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span lang="EN-US" class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Detect</b></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US">– for interactive detection of a sphere to selection.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="p4"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: Sphere detection is controlled by <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Tolerance</b></span> parameter. See <span lang="EN-GB"><a href="../../References/Preferences_-_Datums_-_Detection_Tolerances.htm">System &gt; Preferences &gt; Datums &gt; Detection Tolerances</a></span> <span lang="EN-GB">for details.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span lang="EN-US" class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Tolerances</b></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US">– calls</span> <span lang="EN-GB">System&gt;Preferences&gt;Datums&gt;Detection Tolerances</span> <span lang="EN-US">dialog for settings the detection tolerances.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Choose entity</span>:</b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button – to pick in the viewport an existing sphere. The cursor shape for pick mode is</span><img src="../Images/cursor_pick.gif" width="23px" height="24px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Listbox</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">– to select from the list a predefined sphere.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table-func"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Centre:</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button – to pick the sphere centre</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Edit boxes</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">– to type co-ordinates of the sphere centre and the radius.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Notes</b></span><span lang="EN-US">: In</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>c</b></i></span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>onstrained transformation mode</b></i></span> <span lang="EN-US">t</span>he radius edit box is deactivated, because for the constrained transformation are calculated point correspondences only.</b></p>
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick 4 points</b></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US">– for exact sphere definition by picking 4 points in the viewport. The c</span>ursor shape for pick N mode is <span style="font-style:italic;"><i><img src="../Images/cursor_pickNsphere.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt="">.</i></span> To remove a picked point, press the Alt key and click next to the chosen point in the viewport. The <span lang="EN-US">c</span>ursor shape for remove picked point mode is <img src="../Images/cursor_pick_minus.gif" width="20px" height="15px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt="">.</p>
<p class="normal-table">&#160;</p>
<p class="normal-table"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Detect</b></span> button - to detect a sphere shape by picking 1 or more points on the data surface. <span lang="EN-US">&#160;The cursor shape for Detect mode is <img src="../Images/cursor_detectsphere.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt=""></span>. When 1 point is taken, the button caption changes to "Finish [X pts]", where X is updated according to the number of currently picked points. To remove a picked point, press the Alt key and click next to the chosen point in the viewport. The <span lang="EN-US">c</span>ursor shape for remove picked point mode is <img src="../Images/cursor_pick_minus.gif" width="20px" height="15px" border="0" class="img_whs12" alt="">.</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="sub-head">Temporary Sphere</p>
<p>When all <span lang="EN-US">values are set the new sphere will be visualised in the viewport as temporary entity. There are different types of temporary spheres:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>temporary construction sphere</b></span> - when a <span lang="EN-US">sphere</span> takes part in other entity definition, it appears in the viewport as temporary construction datum (white/black coloured by default). Its appearance can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours &gt; Temporary Construction Datum</b></i></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>current construction sphere</b></span> - the currently edited/selected <span lang="EN-US">sphere</span> appears in the viewport as highlighted temporary datum (light red by default). Its colour can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours &gt; Highlighted</b></i></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="P2"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Notes</b></span>: If the temporary construction datum is currently edited, it appears as highlighted temporary datum.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>final construction sphere</b></span> - when all definition fields/all construction tabs are filled, then the <span lang="EN-US">sphere</span> appears in the viewport as final construction datum (green/black coloured by default). Its appearance can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours &gt; Final Construction Datum.</b></i></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="p3"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Notes</b></span>: If the current construction datum is actually the final one, then it will be coloured as final construction datum.</p>
<p>When this final construction datum is really created then its colour will be changed to the real datum colour (set in <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b><a href="../../References/Display_Settings-Colours.htm">System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours</a></b></i></span> ).</p>
